1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:04,219
All the call controls live in the soft phone.

2
00:00:04,219 --> 00:00:08,954
This video shows how to dial a number and an extension, and describes

3
00:00:08,954 --> 00:00:14,130
how to answer, hold, add a call, transfer and merge calls into a conference.

4
00:00:18,730 --> 00:00:23,061
A phone in the browser must do what a desk phone does:

5
00:00:23,061 --> 00:00:26,670
dial, answer, hold, transfer and conference.

6
00:00:27,420 --> 00:00:32,659
The site used for this video has no connected phone provider, and never places a call.

7
00:00:32,659 --> 00:00:36,759
So the keypad and extension dialing are shown as they are, and the

8
00:00:36,759 --> 00:00:41,030
controls that appear only during a live call are described on slides.

9
00:00:45,231 --> 00:00:46,910
Choose the Keypad tab.

10
00:00:46,910 --> 00:00:50,865
Type the number in international form, starting with a plus.

11
00:00:50,865 --> 00:00:54,881
Or pick the country flag first, and type the national number.

12
00:00:55,336 --> 00:00:59,740
The number is formatted as you type, and turned into a full international

13
00:00:59,740 --> 00:01:01,579
number before it is dialed.

14
00:01:01,579 --> 00:01:04,645
The green Call button, or Enter, places the call.

15
00:01:04,645 --> 00:01:06,596
This video does not press it.

16
00:01:10,796 --> 00:01:15,174
While the number rings, the phone plays a ringback tone in your headset,

17
00:01:15,174 --> 00:01:17,139
and the status reads Ringing.

18
00:01:17,139 --> 00:01:21,236
The tone stops when the other person answers, and the timer starts.

19
00:01:21,986 --> 00:01:25,492
The phone refuses some numbers before anything is dialed:

20
00:01:25,492 --> 00:01:31,058
emergency numbers, premium-rate numbers, and short numbers your administrator has not allowed.

21
00:01:31,058 --> 00:01:33,506
Use another phone for emergency calls.

22
00:01:37,722 --> 00:01:39,496
Click Dial extension.

23
00:01:39,496 --> 00:01:45,542
The country flag disappears, and the field reads Search a name, or enter an extension.

24
00:01:46,011 --> 00:01:49,696
Type an extension number, and the phone shows who it rings.

25
00:01:49,696 --> 00:01:51,341
Or start typing a name:

26
00:01:51,341 --> 00:01:54,686
the people who match are listed with their extension.

27
00:01:54,686 --> 00:01:56,331
Click one to call them.

28
00:01:56,840 --> 00:02:00,398
Click Dial phone number to go back to ordinary numbers.

29
00:02:00,398 --> 00:02:04,482
Extension calls are internal, so do-not-call lists do not apply.

30
00:02:04,482 --> 00:02:08,740
If your colleague does not answer, you are sent to their voicemail.

31
00:02:12,940 --> 00:02:17,680
An incoming call opens the Incoming call window in the soft phone, even

32
00:02:17,680 --> 00:02:19,589
when the panel is closed.

33
00:02:19,589 --> 00:02:25,130
It shows the caller, the queue or who transferred the call, and any matched records.

34
00:02:25,880 --> 00:02:27,878
Answer connects the call.

35
00:02:27,878 --> 00:02:31,100
Answer and open also opens a matched record.

36
00:02:31,100 --> 00:02:36,900
Voicemail sends the caller to voicemail, and Ignore declines the call on this phone.

37
00:02:37,650 --> 00:02:41,926
A call from a queue arrives as an offer first, with a countdown,

38
00:02:41,926 --> 00:02:44,370
in My workspace and the agent bar.

39
00:02:48,570 --> 00:02:51,318
Mute stops the other person hearing you.

40
00:02:51,318 --> 00:02:54,784
Hold puts them on hold, and Resume brings them back.

41
00:02:54,784 --> 00:03:00,400
Keypad sends key presses, for example to pick an option in another company's phone menu.

42
00:03:01,150 --> 00:03:05,384
Hang up ends the selected call, and is the only red button.

43
00:03:05,384 --> 00:03:10,075
With two or more calls, End all ends every call after you confirm,

44
00:03:10,075 --> 00:03:12,290
and Active calls lists them.

45
00:03:13,040 --> 00:03:18,159
Add call puts the current call on hold, and opens the keypad for the second one.

46
00:03:18,159 --> 00:03:21,730
Back to call, or Escape, takes the held call off hold.

47
00:03:25,930 --> 00:03:29,410
Transfer opens the transfer panel in place of the keypad.

48
00:03:29,410 --> 00:03:31,840
Blind sends the call straight to them.

49
00:03:31,840 --> 00:03:35,430
Warm lets you speak to them before the call is handed over.

50
00:03:36,180 --> 00:03:42,570
Pick the destination from the Directory, or type an extension, a name or a phone number.

51
00:03:42,570 --> 00:03:48,280
For a Contact Center call, the panel lists Agents, Queues and Outside numbers.

52
00:03:49,030 --> 00:03:53,494
In a warm transfer, click Complete transfer to hand the caller over, or

53
00:03:53,494 --> 00:03:56,218
Cancel transfer to go back to the caller.

54
00:03:56,218 --> 00:04:01,320
If the person does not answer within thirty seconds, the caller comes back to you.

55
00:04:02,070 --> 00:04:04,902
The buttons depend on your phone system.

56
00:04:04,902 --> 00:04:07,304
Asterisk supports blind transfer.

57
00:04:07,304 --> 00:04:09,890
Telnyx supports the consult as well.

58
00:04:14,090 --> 00:04:19,230
With two or more calls up, tick the calls in Active calls and click Merge calls.

59
00:04:19,230 --> 00:04:24,550
They are listed as a conference, and each participant has their own hang-up button.

60
00:04:25,300 --> 00:04:28,461
Leave drops you out while the others stay connected.

61
00:04:28,461 --> 00:04:31,950
End for all ends the call for everyone, after you confirm.

62
00:04:32,700 --> 00:04:37,808
A queue or campaign call puts you in wrap-up until you complete the activity.

63
00:04:37,808 --> 00:04:41,870
A direct call, or a call you dialed yourself, skips wrap-up.

64
00:04:46,070 --> 00:04:49,070
Calling a customer back from the Recent tab.

65
00:04:49,820 --> 00:04:54,310
Asking a colleague for help, by typing their name in Dial extension.

66
00:04:55,060 --> 00:05:00,390
A warm transfer to a specialist, so the customer does not repeat the story.

67
00:05:01,140 --> 00:05:04,550
A conference with a customer and a manager.

68
00:05:06,550 --> 00:05:12,876
Dial from the keypad or by extension, and use hold, transfer and conference during a call.

69
00:05:12,876 --> 00:05:14,590
Thanks for watching.

